A lane with no partner selects itself as the shuffle source. The exact original code is:
```cpp
unsigned int partner = lane + static_cast<unsigned int>(offset);
bool hasPartner = partner <= 18u;
int source = hasPartner ? static_cast<int>(partner)
                        : static_cast<int>(lane);
float other = __shfl_sync(mask, value, source, 32);
if (hasPartner) {
    value = value + other;
}
```
Every caller is physical lane 0–18, so its own bit is set in `mask = 0x0007ffffu`. All nineteen lanes execute this shuffle unconditionally with the same mask, making the self-source participating without assuming lockstep.

For example, lane 18 at offset 16 computes partner 34, so `hasPartner` is false and source is 18. The shuffle reads its current value, but the addition is skipped: `value` remains unchanged, so its input is not double-counted. The final shuffle reads lane 0’s completed sum and returns it directly; it performs no additional addition.
